    "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes the 4 `LM Eval Humming` CI jobs (B200/H100, Default and Activation FP8/INT8), which have failed in every Full CI run since 2026-10-06.\n\n`nm-testing/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1` (per-tensor FP8) fails to load with `--moe-backend humming`:\n\n```\nhumming/schema/base.py, in _may_process_global_scale\n    assert scale.size(0) == (num_experts or 1)\nAssertionError\n```\n\nSince #56997, the Humming branch of `convert_to_fp8_moe_kernel_format` installs the processed w13 scale on the layer before converting it. For per-tensor checkpoints, `process_fp8_weight_tensor_strategy_moe` has already requantized w13 to one scale per expert (`[E]`). Humming's tensor schema expects one scale per gate/up shard (`[E, 2]`) and calls `scale.view(-1, 2, 1)`, which gives `E/2` rows. Before #56997 it read the on-disk `[E, 2]` parameter.\n\nThis change broadcasts the per-expert scale to both shards. Both shards were requantized to that same scale, so the result is exact.\n\n## Bisect\n\nLast pass: Full CI #93039 (`1e5d0ea888`). First fail: #93187 (`385d86a6cf`). I ran only the B200 Humming Default job on #56997 and on its parent:\n\n- #56997 (`d1f3d8b870`): failed, same assert (https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94436)\n- parent: passed (https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94437)\n\n## Test Plan\n\nRun the Humming LM Eval jobs on this PR.\n\nWanted for v0.32.0 (milestone \"v0.32.0 cherry picks\").\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
